  "content_description": "Action Item - Teams",
  "content_text_body": "There may not realistically be enough resources to get everything done. Teams who think they can accomplish everything often end up getting very little done. The goal is to learn how to prioritize tasks for optimal productivity.\n\n### Create a priority list\n\nAs a group, create a priority list. Decide on what should be done first, second, and third. As new items are added to the team's plate, communicate about how these items will impact other priorities so that the team can stay focused and work coherently. \n\n### Balance speed and quality\n\nPart of prioritizing is determining how quickly a task needs to be done, and the level of quality it requires. Quality can suffer when work is rushed, so for each task aim to identify which is more important at this stage: speed or quality (no, you can't choose both.)",
